Selling a set of 3 plastic storage tote with Hinged Attached Lid. The 3 containers have different sizes: 21in x 15in x 17in (H); 21in x 15in x 12in (H); 21in x 15in x 9in (H);
Product Description
Flip top hinged lid totes are versatile stackable storage containers for your home or business. Great for any sportsman, they hold camping gear, boots, food, boat supplies. Organize seasonal decorations, clothes or bulk supplies. The durable heavy-duty containers protect contents from damage, and the attached lids won't get misplaced. Much more sturdy than cardboard boxes, ALCs make great moving boxes, protecting contents from impact and water damage. Akro-Mils heavy-duty Attached Lid Containers are ideal for distribution and shipping, making great round-trip containers. A hole on both ends of the tote can accommodate zip ties to securely fasten lid closed.

Offering this vintage dune-buggy rear sub-frame as shown.  It appears to be a professional jig-&-mig-weld unit, as witnessed by the previously-removed ID plate on the top of the rear frame tube (Photo 4).
Dimensions are:
51" OAL, not counting add-on bumper guards;
39" wide at front brackets;
Width of 42-1/2" at shock brackets;
Main cradle -- 14" high;
Bottom of cradle to top of shock brackets -- 19-1/2" high;
Radius at rear corners approximately 7";
Main frame tubes -- 1-1/4"; support tubes -- 1";
Lower slotted frame-mount pads -- 5-1/2" tall x 2" wide x 1/4" thick at approximate 30° rearward angle.
The first four pictures show it right-side-up; the next five show it upside-down.  Photo 1 shows it from the driver's (left) side; Photo 2 shows the right side.
I also have a transaxle adapter that fits the early-model (1960-'64) Corvairs.  I'm not sure if it was used with this frame, but it's available, if you want it.
The $495.00 asking price is both fair and firm. Please don't contact me wasting my time and yours trying to haggle on the price. If I wanted a haggle price, I would have listed it for $650.00, and you would have felt good to get it for $495.00.
